infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Plain T[] vs NoInfer<T>[]
  desc One parameter decides T — or every parameter does
  compares
    - label allowed: T[]
      children
        - label Both args feed T
          desc initial and allowed both drive inference
        - label A typo widens T to string
          desc the wrong literal compiles, T becomes string
        - label The list guard evaporates
          desc no error — the typo slips through
    - label allowed: NoInfer<T>[]
      children
        - label Only initial feeds T
          desc allowed is removed as an inference source
        - label T is pinned to the literal
          desc T becomes the exact initial literal
        - label The typo is rejected
          desc a mismatched element fails to type-check
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
